WEBVTT

00:14.700 --> 00:17.500
♪The Upper Three hold the seals♪

00:17.540 --> 00:21.380
♪A valiant general, an opera star, and a ruthless cripple♪

00:21.980 --> 00:24.420
♪The Middle Three stir the clouds♪

00:24.500 --> 00:29.140
♪A fiend, a wandering hero, and a master of the blade♪

00:30.540 --> 00:33.220
♪The Lower Three deal in gold♪

00:33.540 --> 00:37.500
♪A beauty, a seer, and a scholar♪

00:37.860 --> 00:40.780
♪The Upper, Middle, and Lower Three♪

00:41.620 --> 00:49.300
♪Represent the nine houses of old Changsha♪

00:49.900 --> 00:51.380
♪Together, they are known♪

00:52.060 --> 00:56.660
♪As the Mystic Nine♪

01:25.660 --> 01:31.900
[Mystic Nine]
[Adapted from the novel of Kennedy Xu]

01:32.060 --> 01:34.980
[Episode 24]
[This story is purely fictional]

01:54.240 --> 01:55.370
How did someone

01:55.390 --> 01:57.090
get trapped and die inside the wall?

02:00.000 --> 02:00.780
Coward.

02:01.800 --> 02:03.340
You coward!

02:17.200 --> 02:17.740
Master,

02:18.520 --> 02:19.940
he was shot through the heart.

02:35.760 --> 02:36.220
Master.

02:48.200 --> 02:49.020
Does this look familiar?

02:57.550 --> 02:59.090
The whistle you're wearing now

03:00.080 --> 03:01.500
was newly made for you by the Wu Clan.

03:04.760 --> 03:06.410
They said your old one was lost.

03:19.640 --> 03:20.900
The marks you left before

03:20.920 --> 03:22.090
all point here.

03:23.800 --> 03:24.900
Do you remember anything?

03:46.430 --> 03:47.220
I killed him.

03:49.870 --> 03:51.060
Laogou, what are you talking about?

03:51.320 --> 03:52.940
Why would you kill someone for no reason?

03:56.800 --> 03:57.850
To get out,

03:59.390 --> 04:00.590
I killed the men of Unit 401.

04:00.640 --> 04:01.180
Wait.

04:09.710 --> 04:11.010
I know what kind of man Laogou is.

04:12.360 --> 04:13.570
He wouldn't kill innocent people.

04:18.960 --> 04:20.410
How could you possibly

04:20.410 --> 04:22.450
have killed all of Unit 401 by yourself?

04:23.030 --> 04:23.650
And why

04:26.030 --> 04:27.060
was Zhang Yuanhang's body

04:27.120 --> 04:28.060
the only one

04:28.080 --> 04:28.860
buried in the wall?

04:38.910 --> 04:39.740
I killed them.

04:44.030 --> 04:44.810
If you don't die,

04:45.520 --> 04:46.420
I can't get out.

04:46.710 --> 04:48.100
If you don't die, I can't get out!

04:48.790 --> 04:49.620
In a corridor...

04:50.790 --> 04:51.660
Is there someone else

04:51.680 --> 04:52.540
around here?

04:55.080 --> 04:56.010
There are others nearby.

04:56.710 --> 04:57.330
Who?

04:58.350 --> 04:59.250
I can't see their faces.

05:00.520 --> 05:01.570
Before that,

05:03.150 --> 05:04.130
where were you,

05:05.080 --> 05:06.370
and who were you with?

05:18.830 --> 05:19.570
The Japanese.

05:21.030 --> 05:22.250
I was with the Japanese.

05:23.680 --> 05:24.370
I led them

05:24.390 --> 05:25.300
to the Star-Moon Sand.

05:26.350 --> 05:27.210
I led them to it.

05:29.790 --> 05:31.620
Why were you with the Japanese?

05:33.350 --> 05:34.500
Did Yoshiyuki Hatoyama

05:34.520 --> 05:35.540
force you to do something?

05:36.640 --> 05:37.370
Why did I...?

05:39.030 --> 05:39.740
Why did I...?

05:56.880 --> 05:57.370
I...

05:57.680 --> 05:59.100
I left a mark somewhere.

06:00.150 --> 06:01.210
I left other clues.

06:02.790 --> 06:03.940
Let's look for them now.

06:04.080 --> 06:04.570
Master Zhang.

06:06.760 --> 06:07.420
If I really

06:07.440 --> 06:08.180
betrayed you all

06:09.230 --> 06:10.370
and killed the men of Unit 401,

06:13.790 --> 06:15.010
punish me according to the law.

06:17.000 --> 06:17.810
But my brothers and dogs

06:17.830 --> 06:18.660
are innocent.

06:19.760 --> 06:20.500
Could you

06:22.030 --> 06:23.420
spare their lives?

06:27.560 --> 06:28.660
Don't blame yourself yet.

06:31.790 --> 06:32.940
Until we uncover

06:32.960 --> 06:33.770
the whole truth,

06:34.520 --> 06:35.890
none of us should jump to conclusions.

06:36.880 --> 06:37.980
What matters most now

06:38.830 --> 06:40.250
is finding the clues you left

06:40.270 --> 06:41.250
and Yoshiyuki Hatoyama.

07:10.200 --> 07:10.980
This is it.

07:12.030 --> 07:12.540
Tiezui,

07:13.270 --> 07:13.690
your watch.

07:15.080 --> 07:15.620
What?

07:16.030 --> 07:16.660
Give me your watch.

07:18.560 --> 07:19.060
Here.

07:19.680 --> 07:20.250
Here, take it.

07:27.000 --> 07:27.940
This pattern

07:28.120 --> 07:29.540
looks strangely familiar.

07:36.590 --> 07:37.540
I remember now.

07:38.560 --> 07:39.450
The note

07:39.470 --> 07:40.810
we took from Laogou's wound

07:41.080 --> 07:42.100
had the same pattern.

07:44.000 --> 07:46.370
But what does 12:08

07:46.390 --> 07:47.300
mean?

08:33.560 --> 08:34.660
What does this say?

08:42.160 --> 08:43.450
I think I remember something.

08:51.110 --> 08:52.380
The spells are tied to time.

08:53.590 --> 08:55.060
Time is the key to the mystery.

08:58.200 --> 08:59.060
It's time.

09:00.870 --> 09:01.970
Could time be connected

09:01.990 --> 09:03.380
to the secrets of the Xumi Realm?

09:04.630 --> 09:05.730
Otherwise, you wouldn't have

09:06.110 --> 09:07.260
left such a large mark here.

09:07.870 --> 09:08.450
The spells

09:09.750 --> 09:10.690
are tied to time.

09:11.350 --> 09:14.490
Time is the key to the mystery.

09:16.470 --> 09:17.690
Someone told me that.

09:17.960 --> 09:18.300
Then

09:18.590 --> 09:19.400
what exactly

09:19.400 --> 09:20.260
does that mean?

09:22.440 --> 09:23.060
Spells...

09:24.040 --> 09:24.690
Time...

09:27.590 --> 09:28.450
I think I know

09:28.710 --> 09:29.810
how the spells work now.

09:31.830 --> 09:33.260
After I tamed the Zhainiangniang,

09:33.320 --> 09:34.180
Hatoyama brought me here.

09:35.080 --> 09:36.060
To get me to work for him,

09:36.280 --> 09:37.180
he told me everything,

09:37.960 --> 09:38.540
including how

09:38.590 --> 09:39.570
the spells really worked.

09:48.470 --> 09:49.330
This high wall

09:49.800 --> 09:51.020
is exactly like the one in Changsha.

10:21.830 --> 10:24.570
These are the people you and Zhang Qishan

10:24.590 --> 10:25.570
were looking for, right?

10:26.400 --> 10:27.380
Now you've found them.

10:28.590 --> 10:29.780
You can take them away.

11:05.990 --> 11:07.420
What did they do to you?

11:11.080 --> 11:12.260
I'm here to get you out.

11:14.560 --> 11:15.060
Brother?

11:18.350 --> 11:18.780
Brother.

11:19.560 --> 11:20.380
Say something to me.

11:21.590 --> 11:22.420
What happened to all of you?

11:23.470 --> 11:23.970
Talk to me.

11:25.560 --> 11:26.420
What happened

11:26.680 --> 11:27.330
to all of you?

11:29.350 --> 11:30.180
Say something.

11:30.680 --> 11:31.140
Brother.

11:31.870 --> 11:32.450
Talk to me.

11:33.080 --> 11:34.020
Say something!

11:34.440 --> 11:34.900
Brother.

11:36.350 --> 11:36.900
Brother!

11:38.920 --> 11:39.540
How did this happen?

11:42.750 --> 11:43.260
Brother?

11:49.960 --> 11:50.730
How did this happen?

12:18.230 --> 12:18.730
Brother?

12:20.040 --> 12:20.610
Brother?

12:36.630 --> 12:37.490
Quiet.

12:39.680 --> 12:40.540
What in the world...?

12:45.320 --> 12:46.610
Why did he become like this?

12:47.040 --> 12:48.330
What did you do to him?

12:49.510 --> 12:50.610
Have you ever wondered

12:51.590 --> 12:52.690
what kind of creature

12:53.440 --> 12:54.780
you actually tamed?

12:57.470 --> 12:58.020
Monsters

12:59.080 --> 13:00.420
that live in caves.

13:01.440 --> 13:01.850
Go.

13:03.080 --> 13:04.420
Watch how he moves.

13:05.560 --> 13:06.970
And think back to how they moved.

13:07.510 --> 13:09.540
Doesn't he move just like those monsters?

13:23.280 --> 13:24.540
Do you still not understand?

13:25.710 --> 13:26.690
What you tamed

13:28.200 --> 13:29.260
were human beings.

13:34.350 --> 13:35.780
We also captured some

13:35.830 --> 13:36.490
of these creatures here.

13:37.200 --> 13:39.260
The locals call them Zhainiangniang.

13:39.920 --> 13:42.970
In truth, they're all mutated humans.

13:46.870 --> 13:47.570
Right here,

13:48.400 --> 13:49.730
I found the ancient texts

13:49.750 --> 13:50.850
left by Yin Changsheng.

13:52.400 --> 13:53.420
Those texts

13:54.080 --> 13:55.610
record his alchemy.

13:56.200 --> 13:57.420
One of his pills

13:58.080 --> 13:59.420
turns people

13:59.750 --> 14:01.610
into Zhainiangniang after they take it.

14:05.470 --> 14:06.770
I tested it

14:06.770 --> 14:07.770
on a soldier first,

14:09.080 --> 14:10.610
hoping it would work.

14:11.160 --> 14:11.850
So,

14:12.830 --> 14:14.420
the Zhainiangniang you had me tame

14:15.710 --> 14:16.970
were fully mutated...

14:17.470 --> 14:18.330
That's right.

14:20.280 --> 14:23.020
Yin Changsheng practiced alchemy in the Xumi Realm

14:23.350 --> 14:25.900
and created quite a few Zhainiangniang.

14:31.990 --> 14:32.570
So,

14:33.680 --> 14:34.900
all these Unit 401 soldiers

14:36.280 --> 14:37.490
will turn into monsters too?

14:46.830 --> 14:47.380
Take a look.

14:54.800 --> 14:55.900
Yin Changsheng

14:56.510 --> 14:57.770
used them

14:58.080 --> 14:59.490
as a barrier between the Xumi Realm

14:59.630 --> 15:00.820
and the outside world.

15:02.000 --> 15:04.300
He gathered large numbers of Zhainiangniang

15:04.790 --> 15:05.770
around the perimeter

15:05.790 --> 15:07.250
of the Otherworld Tower's core area.

15:07.510 --> 15:08.370
It's filled

15:08.480 --> 15:10.250
with the same toxic gas as the forest.

15:11.200 --> 15:12.850
No outsider can possibly get through.

15:14.440 --> 15:15.890
I need your help

15:17.000 --> 15:18.650
to get us through the toxic gas

15:19.150 --> 15:20.850
and into the depths of the Xumi Realm,

15:22.000 --> 15:22.820
so we can

15:24.840 --> 15:25.770
find this.

15:29.120 --> 15:30.980
This jar is empty now.

15:31.720 --> 15:33.890
I need you to help me find

15:34.120 --> 15:36.370
what used to fill it.

15:37.240 --> 15:38.610
It's called Star-Moon Sand.

15:39.240 --> 15:40.980
It's in the deepest part of the Xumi Realm.

15:43.790 --> 15:45.340
Help me find the Star-Moon Sand,

15:45.870 --> 15:47.770
and I'll release you and Unit 401 at once.

15:48.200 --> 15:49.460
I'll also give you the antidote

15:50.910 --> 15:52.490
to stop that soldier from mutating.

16:06.550 --> 16:07.700
The terrain here is too complicated.

16:09.360 --> 16:10.370
It's a complete maze.

16:11.510 --> 16:11.940
I

16:13.240 --> 16:13.820
can't do it.

16:14.080 --> 16:15.460
The Zhainiangniang can find it!

16:18.390 --> 16:20.770
You just need to make them

16:21.480 --> 16:22.420
a little more obedient

16:23.270 --> 16:23.980
and have them lead the way.

16:24.750 --> 16:26.250
Then they'll find the Star-Moon Sand.

16:26.790 --> 16:28.180
Zhainiangniang aren't dogs.

16:29.000 --> 16:30.340
It's hard enough keeping them from attacking people!

16:33.720 --> 16:34.610
Don't you have dogs?

16:35.720 --> 16:37.220
Why not have them find it for you?

16:47.320 --> 16:48.770
There is actually

16:49.270 --> 16:50.980
some Star-Moon Sand inside this tower,

16:52.150 --> 16:53.490
but activating those jars

16:54.320 --> 16:55.650
requires sand

16:56.360 --> 16:57.580
of extremely high purity.

17:30.790 --> 17:31.460
See?

17:32.350 --> 17:33.900
Even Star-Moon Sand of this quality

17:34.310 --> 17:35.090
drives dogs into a frenzy

17:35.310 --> 17:36.980
as soon as they smell it.

17:37.160 --> 17:39.460
Only the Zhainiangniang are immune to it.

17:40.550 --> 17:41.140
Why?

17:41.830 --> 17:44.250
Because Star-Moon Sand is actually

17:44.270 --> 17:45.730
formed from scales

17:46.000 --> 17:48.250
shed by the Zhainiangniang over time.

17:49.590 --> 17:50.860
Over many years, the scales

17:51.640 --> 17:53.140
are weathered and gradually condense

17:53.920 --> 17:55.290
into Star-Moon Sand.

18:00.920 --> 18:02.090
Amazing, isn't it?

18:03.480 --> 18:05.420
When Yin Changsheng's pills

18:05.440 --> 18:06.460
are given to humans,

18:06.510 --> 18:07.530
they mutate

18:07.640 --> 18:09.140
into Zhainiangniang.

18:09.400 --> 18:11.460
Then the substances shed by the Zhainiangniang

18:11.640 --> 18:13.330
become Star-Moon Sand,

18:13.480 --> 18:14.570
and Star-Moon Sand

18:14.750 --> 18:16.140
is the key

18:16.160 --> 18:19.180
to making Yin Changsheng's spells come true!

18:20.640 --> 18:21.700
Didn't you say

18:22.310 --> 18:23.530
it was caused by hallucinations?

18:24.270 --> 18:25.180
Hallucinations?

18:25.550 --> 18:26.250
No...

18:27.000 --> 18:28.730
Those weren't illusions at all.

18:29.680 --> 18:30.900
How could they possibly be?

18:31.680 --> 18:32.620
Traveling through time,

18:33.310 --> 18:34.420
bringing the dead back to life,

18:34.680 --> 18:35.530
and seeing the future.

18:35.590 --> 18:36.380
What kind of illusion

18:36.400 --> 18:37.250
could do any of that?

18:37.830 --> 18:38.770
These things actually

18:38.830 --> 18:39.810
happened.

18:40.440 --> 18:42.290
Didn't you experience them yourself?

18:44.110 --> 18:44.770
Help me.

18:46.550 --> 18:47.250
If you help me,

18:48.310 --> 18:49.530
I'll release Unit 401.

18:51.440 --> 18:53.090
For every day you delay,

18:53.880 --> 18:55.220
I'll use

18:55.270 --> 18:57.700
another Unit 401 soldier as a test subject

18:58.070 --> 18:58.980
until I've

18:59.000 --> 19:00.730
used them all up.

19:02.830 --> 19:03.700
Once you find it,

19:04.720 --> 19:05.460
what will you do with it?

19:06.110 --> 19:08.220
Use it to win the war, of course.

19:17.400 --> 19:19.010
I'd rather die than help you.

19:20.400 --> 19:21.180
Look over there.

19:26.400 --> 19:27.660
See how he's suffering.

19:30.880 --> 19:31.980
If you're so determined,

19:34.750 --> 19:36.460
then end his life yourself and put him out

19:37.200 --> 19:38.180
of his misery.

20:09.000 --> 20:09.660
Star-Moon Sand.

20:10.750 --> 20:11.490
It's Star-Moon Sand.

20:11.720 --> 20:12.660
Everything Hatoyama

20:12.680 --> 20:14.140
did in the Otherworld Tower

20:14.960 --> 20:16.250
was for the Star-Moon Sand?

20:16.920 --> 20:17.460
That's right.

20:19.440 --> 20:20.730
I train dogs. I know

20:21.880 --> 20:23.050
what Hatoyama's hound's reaction

20:23.070 --> 20:23.770
meant.

20:24.640 --> 20:25.660
It had lost its memory

20:26.400 --> 20:27.530
and forgotten its master.

20:28.880 --> 20:30.090
That's why it became frightened

20:30.510 --> 20:31.180
and agitated.

20:33.550 --> 20:34.770
The Star-Moon Sand in that jar

20:35.030 --> 20:36.660
can make animals lose their memories.

20:37.270 --> 20:38.420
But we inhaled it too.

20:39.440 --> 20:40.140
Why

20:40.160 --> 20:41.050
didn't we lose our memories?

20:44.350 --> 20:44.980
Those dogs

20:45.400 --> 20:46.810
didn't lose all their memories either.

20:47.510 --> 20:48.380
They still remembered

20:48.400 --> 20:49.180
how to follow commands,

20:50.310 --> 20:51.570
but they no longer recognized their masters.

20:52.590 --> 20:53.810
Could we be the same?

20:54.750 --> 20:55.770
We inhaled Star-Moon Sand

20:56.200 --> 20:57.250
inside the Otherworld Tower

20:58.310 --> 20:59.620
and then forgot certain things.

21:01.310 --> 21:01.900
Master Zhang,

21:02.110 --> 21:03.140
what did we forget

21:03.640 --> 21:04.460
in the Otherworld Tower?

21:04.720 --> 21:06.050
My memory seems perfectly intact.

21:06.110 --> 21:06.810
When the human brain

21:07.790 --> 21:09.090
loses a piece of memory,

21:10.200 --> 21:11.330
it fills the gap with imagination.

21:11.960 --> 21:13.460
So the brain can never realize

21:13.720 --> 21:14.810
what it's forgotten.

21:17.200 --> 21:18.350
Sometimes, you feel certain

21:18.350 --> 21:19.730
that something happened.

21:20.240 --> 21:21.050
But when you check the records,

21:21.070 --> 21:21.900
you may find that it

21:21.920 --> 21:22.730
never happened at all.

21:24.310 --> 21:25.900
That's how the brain fills in the gaps.

21:27.480 --> 21:28.460
What did we forget

21:28.480 --> 21:29.380
inside the Otherworld Tower?

21:30.920 --> 21:31.570
Good heavens.

21:32.830 --> 21:34.180
We forgot time itself.

21:34.790 --> 21:35.770
What do you mean?

21:35.920 --> 21:36.530
We forgot

21:36.550 --> 21:37.530
the order of events

21:38.400 --> 21:39.040
and mixed up

21:39.910 --> 21:40.500
the past,

21:40.910 --> 21:41.950
the future, and the present.

21:42.920 --> 21:43.490
We also forgot

21:43.510 --> 21:44.900
how much time had passed.

21:56.350 --> 21:57.140
I understand.

21:58.590 --> 21:59.290
I understand now!

22:00.000 --> 22:00.700
Don't be fooled by appearances.

22:01.000 --> 22:02.140
There aren't countless Otherworld Towers.

22:02.550 --> 22:03.220
There's only

22:03.440 --> 22:04.700
one Otherworld Tower in Changsha.

22:06.640 --> 22:07.900
We've been fooled by time.

22:09.790 --> 22:11.140
What do you mean, Laogou?

22:11.640 --> 22:13.220
We know there's only one Otherworld Tower in Changsha.

22:13.640 --> 22:15.180
How did time fool us?

22:15.550 --> 22:16.810
We're the ones with the problem.

22:18.680 --> 22:20.140
There's only one Otherworld Tower in Changsha,

22:20.270 --> 22:20.860
but there are

22:22.510 --> 22:23.380
countless versions of us.

22:24.750 --> 22:25.380
Laogou,

22:25.440 --> 22:27.090
can you not talk in riddles?

22:28.400 --> 22:29.050
Tell me.

22:29.920 --> 22:30.570
How many times have we

22:30.590 --> 22:31.330
entered the Otherworld Tower?

22:31.590 --> 22:32.660
How many could there be?

22:33.160 --> 22:34.140
Just once.

22:34.200 --> 22:34.770
No.

22:37.070 --> 22:38.380
It wasn't just once.

22:40.880 --> 22:42.330
We entered it countless times.

22:42.590 --> 22:43.180
Exactly.

22:46.160 --> 22:47.570
Every time we left the Otherworld Tower,

22:48.590 --> 22:49.570
we forgot everything.

22:56.830 --> 22:58.050
We all believed

22:59.110 --> 23:00.220
we'd never entered it before,

23:01.070 --> 23:02.460
so we'd go back inside

23:02.960 --> 23:04.250
and repeat everything we'd already done.

23:05.270 --> 23:06.490
Every time we entered,

23:06.720 --> 23:07.900
we were searching for Unit 401.

23:08.550 --> 23:09.370
But once we caught up with them,

23:09.370 --> 23:10.220
we'd forget it all.

23:10.560 --> 23:12.250
Only the memory of pursuing them would remain.

23:12.680 --> 23:13.830
That's why we could never catch them.

23:16.720 --> 23:17.770
Think back carefully.

23:18.720 --> 23:19.570
Inside the tower,

23:20.310 --> 23:21.220
didn't it seem like we never

23:21.240 --> 23:22.180
ate or slept at all?

23:22.590 --> 23:23.050
That's right.

23:24.510 --> 23:25.180
And there were

23:25.880 --> 23:27.290
those wounds that appeared from nowhere.

23:35.160 --> 23:36.220
But we did eat.

23:37.070 --> 23:37.980
And we did get hurt.

23:38.350 --> 23:39.900
When did you hurt your hand?

23:40.960 --> 23:42.730
I... I don't know.

23:43.640 --> 23:44.900
We've lost all those memories.

23:46.510 --> 23:47.250
Our memories

23:47.270 --> 23:47.940
are all wrong,

23:48.550 --> 23:49.330
all jumbled up.

23:49.960 --> 23:51.380
And we never even realized it.

23:52.240 --> 23:53.530
So we pieced those false memories

23:53.920 --> 23:54.660
together

23:54.790 --> 23:56.180
and took them as one complete memory.

23:56.920 --> 23:58.180
So our memories

23:58.920 --> 24:00.490
were pieced together from countless trips

24:00.790 --> 24:01.900
into the Otherworld Tower.

24:07.680 --> 24:08.290
Laogou,

24:09.790 --> 24:10.730
then how did Xiangu and the others

24:11.030 --> 24:12.380
come back from the dead?

24:12.750 --> 24:13.730
It had to do with a candle ritual.

24:15.350 --> 24:16.490
I remember some of it.

24:17.720 --> 24:18.620
We were convinced the shadow

24:18.640 --> 24:19.290
was behind the door.

24:22.510 --> 24:23.780
We decided to make it think

24:23.860 --> 24:24.860
its plan had worked.

24:25.240 --> 24:26.540
They fell for it. They're dying.

24:26.820 --> 24:27.940
To fool it,

24:28.700 --> 24:29.680
I pretended to grieve.

24:30.440 --> 24:31.330
That memory

24:32.160 --> 24:33.660
then got mixed with another one.

24:35.530 --> 24:36.480
Burn Candles to Prolong Life.

24:38.200 --> 24:39.140
Ascend to Heaven.

24:40.640 --> 24:41.490
Peer into the Future.

24:42.550 --> 24:43.860
I'll light these candles,

24:44.830 --> 24:45.730
but my people

24:46.640 --> 24:48.250
must all be returned to me.

24:51.480 --> 24:52.420
My mind filled in the gap

24:52.880 --> 24:54.250
with me bringing my companions back to life.

24:55.400 --> 24:56.090
As for the magic

24:56.110 --> 24:57.250
we thought we'd seen,

24:58.070 --> 24:59.380
it was just the result of us inhaling

24:59.920 --> 25:01.050
Star-Moon Sand in the tower,

25:01.640 --> 25:02.290
losing our memories,

25:03.200 --> 25:04.140
piecing together

25:04.160 --> 25:04.980
separate events,

25:05.830 --> 25:06.770
and hallucinating.

25:18.160 --> 25:18.620
That's it?

25:19.070 --> 25:19.490
That's it.

25:20.200 --> 25:20.900
That's all?

25:24.200 --> 25:24.860
Where's the door?

25:25.720 --> 25:26.380
Why hasn't it opened?

25:40.480 --> 25:41.770
Before the waterway collapsed,

25:42.510 --> 25:43.730
we'd really found a hidden door.

25:45.720 --> 25:46.570
There's a hidden door.

25:49.000 --> 25:50.050
Stay here and stand by.

25:50.590 --> 25:51.140
Yes.

25:52.350 --> 25:53.380
So, Laogou, you mean,

25:53.590 --> 25:54.730
though it looked like my ritual

25:54.920 --> 25:56.330
sent Master Zhang instantly from Liunian Hall

25:56.350 --> 25:57.180
to the Underworld,

25:57.310 --> 25:59.220
the truth is that the ritual

25:59.240 --> 26:00.050
triggered a mechanism?

26:00.240 --> 26:01.120
So that's what happened.

26:01.590 --> 26:02.720
We lost the memory of finding

26:02.720 --> 26:03.510
the hidden door.

26:04.330 --> 26:05.950
Then how did Fifth Master get transported?

26:07.480 --> 26:08.220
Was that whole process

26:08.240 --> 26:09.250
something we imagined?

26:09.510 --> 26:10.530
The part we've forgotten

26:12.370 --> 26:13.980
was from another trip into the tower.

26:14.350 --> 26:14.900
Tiezui,

26:15.590 --> 26:16.250
perform the ritual for me.

26:17.270 --> 26:18.420
If I really don't come back,

26:19.790 --> 26:20.940
follow Eighth Master's lead in civil matters.

26:22.400 --> 26:23.090
For martial affairs,

26:25.720 --> 26:26.620
follow Miss Huo's lead.

26:30.720 --> 26:31.620
And at first,

26:32.160 --> 26:33.460
none of you noticed Xiangu,

26:33.480 --> 26:33.900
did you?

26:34.720 --> 26:35.380
Then suddenly,

26:35.400 --> 26:36.220
everyone knew she was there.

26:36.590 --> 26:37.940
Don't you think something is missing?

26:38.200 --> 26:39.220
Tiezui, perform the ritual.

26:40.030 --> 26:40.490
Laogou...

26:40.510 --> 26:41.140
- Stop dawdling! - I...

26:42.160 --> 26:42.660
Hurry.

26:51.030 --> 26:51.570
Laogou,

26:53.270 --> 26:54.620
what about the hand on the ceiling?

26:54.880 --> 26:56.530
That came from two separate memories

26:57.030 --> 26:57.810
from two different

26:57.830 --> 26:58.620
trips down there.

26:59.310 --> 27:00.290
Master Zhang disappeared.

27:00.830 --> 27:01.900
We split up to search,

27:02.350 --> 27:03.770
but neither side could reach the other.

27:04.400 --> 27:05.660
Only a narrow gap connected us.

27:06.550 --> 27:07.620
I gave Xiangu the button I found

27:07.680 --> 27:08.420
from Master Zhang.

27:09.200 --> 27:10.660
At the time, she didn't trust Master Zhang,

27:11.240 --> 27:12.050
so those memories were stitched

27:12.070 --> 27:12.900
into something strange.

27:16.270 --> 27:17.620
But why didn't we

27:17.640 --> 27:18.570
notice

27:19.270 --> 27:20.320
that everyone's memories

27:20.320 --> 27:21.220
had been altered?

27:21.720 --> 27:23.090
Because we never

27:23.110 --> 27:24.890
put everyone's memories together

27:24.890 --> 27:25.770
and compared them.

27:26.590 --> 27:28.180
It's possible that from the very beginning,

27:28.830 --> 27:30.570
we all remembered things differently.

27:30.960 --> 27:31.530
Exactly.

27:32.480 --> 27:33.490
There's another possibility.

27:34.640 --> 27:35.490
Some emotions,

27:36.480 --> 27:37.180
like fear,

27:37.750 --> 27:39.180
can make us dread the same outcome

27:39.830 --> 27:40.620
and instinctively

27:40.640 --> 27:41.530
expect the worst.

27:42.480 --> 27:43.250
In the end,

27:43.880 --> 27:44.980
the events themselves become blurred,

27:45.790 --> 27:47.220
while the fear

27:48.110 --> 27:49.290
gets etched into our bones.

27:50.350 --> 27:51.460
Everything we imagined,

27:52.200 --> 27:53.220
everything that really happened,

27:53.830 --> 27:54.730
and all the overlapping memories

27:54.750 --> 27:55.530
from each trip

27:57.240 --> 27:58.900
got mixed together.

28:19.340 --> 28:20.820
[You've entered the Otherworld Tower countless times.]

28:20.880 --> 28:22.730
"You've entered the Otherworld Tower countless times.

28:27.510 --> 28:29.010
Here's the secret of the Otherworld Tower's spells:

28:30.030 --> 28:31.140
everything you've experienced

28:31.200 --> 28:33.140
is both real and false.

28:34.160 --> 28:35.700
They are all your memories.

28:36.590 --> 28:38.860
The sand makes your memory lie to you."

28:42.070 --> 28:42.770
I remember now.

28:43.550 --> 28:44.420
We must have

28:45.240 --> 28:46.250
entered the Otherworld Tower

28:47.070 --> 28:48.010
for who knows

28:48.030 --> 28:49.090
how many times.

28:52.600 --> 28:54.480
The Otherworld Patriarch was never real.

28:54.620 --> 28:55.550
Someone posed as him

28:55.970 --> 28:57.460
a few times to guide me.

29:05.440 --> 29:06.490
This morning glory must also be

29:06.510 --> 29:07.900
a mark I left for myself.

29:12.550 --> 29:13.140
Listen.

29:13.880 --> 29:14.620
Let's split up and search.

29:14.880 --> 29:15.700
In one incense stick's time,

29:16.000 --> 29:16.660
we'll meet back here.

30:42.500 --> 30:43.540
[Hua Clan of Xishan]

30:43.540 --> 30:44.900
[Fang Zhongli of Rongjiang]

30:44.900 --> 30:49.140
[Jiangning Embroidery Workshop, Lin Lanqing]

30:57.140 --> 31:00.100
[Workshop owner Lin Lanqing]

31:00.100 --> 31:02.100
[The workshop rushed a silk order for the Imperial Household Department]

31:07.700 --> 31:08.980
[Artisans fled]

31:08.980 --> 31:13.660
[Favored by the Otherworld Patriarch]

31:22.480 --> 31:23.490
That dream of the afterlife

31:24.550 --> 31:26.090
was only the life story of a believer.

31:26.880 --> 31:27.700
I turned it

31:27.720 --> 31:29.050
into a false memory of my past life.

31:34.200 --> 31:34.900
All of this

31:36.070 --> 31:37.620
was a trap set by Yoshiyuki Hatoyama.

31:39.070 --> 31:41.010
He truly knows Star-Moon Sand well.

31:42.110 --> 31:43.180
He laid one trap after another,

31:44.110 --> 31:45.570
drawing us deeper and deeper,

31:46.960 --> 31:48.380
and throwing our memories into chaos

31:49.200 --> 31:50.180
until we couldn't recover

31:50.830 --> 31:51.860
a trace of what really happened.

32:04.030 --> 32:04.860
Good.

32:05.960 --> 32:07.050
Take his men away.

32:08.110 --> 32:09.180
Given Wu Laogou's temperament,

32:10.030 --> 32:11.620
he must have lost control by now.

32:12.790 --> 32:13.700
Find a way to get him

32:14.030 --> 32:16.700
and Zhang Qishan away from the group.

32:38.880 --> 32:41.050
If Wu Laogou wants to save them,

32:41.680 --> 32:45.010
he'll have to go deep into the Otherworld Tower.

32:46.590 --> 32:47.660
He didn't have to

32:47.920 --> 32:51.810
put himself in such danger.

32:52.720 --> 32:53.660
All of this

32:54.070 --> 32:55.180
is because he agreed

32:55.790 --> 32:57.330
to help Zhang Qishan.

33:03.900 --> 33:04.900
The deeper he goes,

33:04.940 --> 33:05.980
the worse the poisoning gets,

33:06.150 --> 33:08.940
and the more his memory gets scrambled.

33:12.070 --> 33:12.980
So,

33:13.510 --> 33:15.420
inside Changsha's Otherworld Tower,

33:15.890 --> 33:17.530
we made up a complete story

33:17.550 --> 33:18.770
of our exploration.

33:19.590 --> 33:20.330
We filled in the gaps

33:20.640 --> 33:22.090
in our memories with imagination.

33:22.750 --> 33:23.900
No wonder

33:24.750 --> 33:25.490
we seemed to go instantly

33:26.030 --> 33:26.810
from Liunian Hall

33:26.830 --> 33:27.730
to the great ghost palace,

33:28.350 --> 33:29.250
yet we could never find

33:29.270 --> 33:30.330
any flaw in those mechanisms.

33:30.880 --> 33:31.770
Yin Changsheng

33:32.160 --> 33:33.140
and the Otherworld Patriarch

33:33.880 --> 33:34.980
must have used

33:35.110 --> 33:36.050
these confused memories

33:36.590 --> 33:38.180
to create their so-called magic.

33:38.830 --> 33:39.620
When Hatoyama

33:39.640 --> 33:40.620
brought me here,

33:41.510 --> 33:42.660
I suddenly realized

33:43.350 --> 33:43.860
that here,

33:44.400 --> 33:45.620
the towers went on endlessly.

33:46.440 --> 33:47.250
But in Changsha,

33:48.110 --> 33:49.490
we were the ones caught in a loop.

33:55.200 --> 33:56.730
That's why you drew

33:56.790 --> 33:57.940
such a huge clock face here.

33:59.960 --> 34:02.220
Time is the key to the mystery.

34:02.750 --> 34:05.220
It was all caused by inhaling Star-Moon Sand.

34:06.310 --> 34:07.860
So Yin Changsheng's spells

34:08.670 --> 34:09.380
were fake,

34:09.550 --> 34:10.380
nothing but tricks.

34:10.880 --> 34:11.650
Then what about Ding Qiansui?

34:12.110 --> 34:13.210
He wasn't in the Otherworld Tower.

34:13.590 --> 34:15.340
We saw him die from magic ourselves.

34:15.510 --> 34:16.570
Zhang Qishan,

34:18.070 --> 34:20.260
you think far too highly of yourself.

34:20.630 --> 34:21.980
Since I know

34:22.070 --> 34:23.900
how the magic works,

34:24.590 --> 34:25.940
I can

34:26.800 --> 34:28.780
reverse time itself!

34:33.230 --> 34:34.300
The Star-Moon Sand he used

34:34.920 --> 34:36.050
still affected you.

34:36.960 --> 34:37.820
Your memory became confused,

34:38.400 --> 34:39.460
and you let Ding Qiansui go.

34:46.150 --> 34:47.610
But the mutated shadow killed him.

34:48.800 --> 34:49.340
His body was made to look

34:49.360 --> 34:50.380
as though he'd been disemboweled.

34:51.150 --> 34:52.610
They used Star-Moon Sand to control your guards

34:53.190 --> 34:54.340
and had them bring the body back.

34:54.960 --> 34:56.050
Those two memories were pieced together,

34:56.550 --> 34:57.900
making it seem the magic had worked.

35:07.320 --> 35:08.490
Then are we still

35:08.510 --> 35:09.780
under the effects of Star-Moon Sand?

35:09.840 --> 35:10.900
Star-Moon Sand only appears

35:11.190 --> 35:12.090
where spells are being used.

35:12.480 --> 35:13.340
Even if there is some here,

35:14.110 --> 35:15.050
we've already been exposed.

35:15.670 --> 35:16.420
It's too late to cover up now.

35:17.670 --> 35:18.530
As I remember it,

35:19.440 --> 35:20.300
Yoshiyuki Hatoyama

35:20.880 --> 35:22.210
was barely affected by Star-Moon Sand.

35:22.510 --> 35:23.170
That means

35:23.630 --> 35:24.460
he already found

35:24.880 --> 35:26.090
a way to neutralize its effects.

35:26.550 --> 35:27.420
Ultimately,

35:27.880 --> 35:28.860
it all comes down

35:29.630 --> 35:31.420
to Star-Moon Sand,

35:31.800 --> 35:32.340
the scales

35:32.400 --> 35:33.900
shed by Zhainiangniang.

35:34.710 --> 35:35.490
It can throw memories

35:35.510 --> 35:36.260
into chaos

35:36.360 --> 35:37.340
and even cause hallucinations.

35:38.480 --> 35:40.170
But it gets used up very quickly.

35:41.230 --> 35:42.820
Yoshiyuki Hatoyama was trying to reach

35:42.880 --> 35:43.820
the Xumi Realm's

35:43.880 --> 35:45.130
innermost chamber

35:46.230 --> 35:47.340
because inside that chamber

35:47.880 --> 35:49.650
was a large amount of what he wanted:

35:50.320 --> 35:51.530
Star-Moon Sand.

36:09.180 --> 36:13.340
♪The past fades like smoke♪

36:13.700 --> 36:16.420
♪A choice is made in silence♪

36:16.700 --> 36:19.500
♪In this labyrinthine puzzle♪

36:19.900 --> 36:23.660
♪Who can reach the shore?♪

36:23.900 --> 36:27.340
♪Just an ordinary farewell♪

36:27.620 --> 36:31.020
♪The sun seems to shine bright over our heads♪

36:31.100 --> 36:38.380
♪But this could be our last trip together♪

36:38.820 --> 36:42.100
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

36:42.380 --> 36:45.620
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

36:45.780 --> 36:49.820
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

36:50.020 --> 36:53.380
♪Who believes in fate?♪

36:53.620 --> 36:56.980
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

36:57.220 --> 37:00.500
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

37:00.820 --> 37:04.500
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

37:04.700 --> 37:07.940
♪Take care♪

37:07.940 --> 37:10.500
♪We once raced♪

37:10.580 --> 37:12.500
♪For the dawn♪

37:12.660 --> 37:15.940
♪Ever-lasting bond, a satisfying vindication♪

37:16.060 --> 37:19.340
♪In the web of fate♪

37:19.340 --> 37:22.540
♪No one can escape♪

37:23.540 --> 37:25.380
♪Life and death cut like a blade♪

37:25.540 --> 37:27.100
♪We too were young once♪

37:27.180 --> 37:30.620
♪Fortunate to brave the raging waves together♪

37:30.820 --> 37:33.140
♪Keep the ember lit♪

37:33.260 --> 37:37.780
♪To illuminate the journey ahead♪

37:37.900 --> 37:40.860
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

37:41.100 --> 37:44.620
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

37:44.740 --> 37:48.500
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

37:48.820 --> 37:52.300
♪Who believes in fate?♪

37:52.460 --> 37:55.460
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

37:55.700 --> 37:59.460
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

37:59.620 --> 38:03.340
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

38:03.460 --> 38:14.900
♪Please, do take care of yourself♪
